    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Whether crowned by birth, chosen by the people, or simply the one others turn to when hard decisions must be made, you lead. Your regalia marks the kind of ruler you are, your court shapes the people who follow you, and your loyal follower fights at your side.</em></p><p><strong>Key Attribute</strong> Charisma</p><p><strong>Hit Points</strong> 8 plus your Constitution modifier</p><hr /><h2>Initial Proficiencies</h2><p><strong>Perception</strong> Expert</p><p><strong>Saving Throws</strong> Trained in Fortitude, expert in Reflex, expert in Will</p><p><strong>Skills</strong> Trained in Society and 2 skills defined by your sovereign's court; trained in a number of additional skills equal to 2 plus your Intelligence modifier</p><p><strong>Attacks</strong> Trained in simple weapons, martial weapons, and unarmed attacks</p><p><strong>Defenses</strong> Trained in light and medium armor and unarmored defense</p><p><strong>Class DC</strong> Trained in sovereign class DC</p><hr /><h2>Sidebar: A Ruler By Any Other Name</h2><p>The sovereign's story does not have to be about kings, queens, or inherited power. A sovereign might instead be an elected ruler, the leader of a church, a revolutionary organizer, or simply the person others trust when difficult decisions must be made. Their authority comes from service, competence, responsibility, or the confidence of their people. The fantasy is not that they were born to lead; it is that they chose to.</p>"
    },
